    "result_text": "The build succeeds and all tests pass. Here's what I implemented.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `POST /api/owners` pipeline now honors an optional `Idempotency-Key` header: a repeat create with an already-seen key returns the originally created owner with **200** instead of creating a duplicate (which would otherwise fail the identity check with 409).\n\nFollowing the project's OfficeFloor function-injection convention (no `@RestController`, one small function class per step, state via `Out<T>`/`@Val`, branching via `@Flow`), I added:\n\n**New function classes** (`rest/function/owner/`):\n- `IdempotencyStore` \u2014 a `@Component` bean mapping key \u2192 created owner id (lives beyond the request transaction so committed creates stay idempotent).\n- `IdempotencyKey` \u2014 a small record carrying the header value (possibly `null`) between steps by type.\n- `CheckIdempotentCreate` \u2014 new first step. Reads `@RequestHeader(name = \"Idempotency-Key\", required = false)`; if the key was already used and its owner still exists, it publishes that owner and invokes the `@Flow(\"existing\")` branch (which suppresses `next:`, per OfficeFloor semantics) to respond 200. Otherwise it returns normally and the pipeline proceeds to validation. It always publishes the key for the recording step.\n- `ExistingOwnerFlow` \u2014 the `@FunctionalInterface` for that branch.\n- `RecordIdempotentCreate` \u2014 runs right after `SaveOwner` (so the id exists), recording key \u2192 owner id; a keyless request is a no-op.\n\n**YAML wiring** (`owners.POST.yml`): added `checkIdempotency` as the entry step (`next: validate`, `outputs: { existing: respondExisting }`), a `respondExisting` step reusing the existing `RespondWithOwner` responder (200 + `OwnerDto`), and `recordIdempotency` between `save` and `audit`. All steps carry `govern: [ transaction ]` like the rest of the pipeline.\n\nRequests without the header fall straight through to the normal create flow, so existing behavior is unchanged \u2014 confirmed by the full suite passing.",
