    "probe_text": "I now have the full picture. Here's the complete, ordered account.\n\n## Validations and side-effects when creating an owner via `POST /api/owners`\n\n**Endpoint guard (before any step):** the whole file requires `hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`. The entire pipeline runs inside a single transaction (`govern: [ transaction ]` on every step), committing once at the end.\n\n### 1. `CheckIdempotentCreate` \u2014 idempotency short-circuit\n- Reads the optional `Idempotency-Key` header and publishes it (null if absent) for later recording.\n- If a non-blank key has already been recorded **and** its owner still exists, it publishes that original owner and branches to `respondExisting` \u2192 responds **200** with the original owner, creating nothing further.\n- Otherwise (no key, key unseen, or original owner gone) it continues to validation.\n\n### 2. `ValidateOwnerFields` \u2014 the body validation (reads `@RequestBody` once)\nApplied in this order:\n- **Address normalization first:** normalizes `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` and flat `address` (trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`). If `addressLine1` is present, the structured form is composed into `address` (preferred over the flat field).\n- **Required-field check:** `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone` must be non-null and non-blank *after normalization*; any missing \u2192 **400** (`MissingOwnerFieldsException`) naming the offending fields.\n- **Telephone normalization to E.164:** strips separators, keeps explicit `+` country code or assumes `+61` (dropping one leading `0`); must be 8\u201315 digits, and recognised country codes must have the exact national length (`+61`\u21929, `+1`\u219210); otherwise **400** (`InvalidOwnerTelephoneException`). The normalized value is stored on the body.\n- **Email normalization (only if present):** must match the syntax pattern (\u2192 **400** `InvalidOwnerEmailException`); domain must not be on the disposable blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`) (\u2192 **400** `DisposableOwnerEmailException`); stored lower-cased. Absent email allowed.\n- **Postcode validation (only if present):** must be exactly 4 digits and, for a city with a known region (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099), fall in range; otherwise **400** (`InvalidOwnerPostcodeException`). Absent postcode allowed.\n- **Registration date:** if supplied, must not be after the server date; otherwise **400** (`FutureRegistrationDateException`).\n- Publishes the validated body.\n\n### 3. `EnsureUniqueOwnerIdentity` \u2014 household duplicate block\n- Computes the deterministic `householdId` (first 12 hex of SHA-256 of `normalizedLastName|postcode`).\n- If any non-soft-deleted existing owner already carries that `householdId` \u2192 **409** (`DuplicateOwnerIdentityException`).\n- Bypassed when the request sets `sharesHousehold`, or when there is no postcode (no household).\n\n### 4. `EnsureCityCapacity` \u2014 city capacity block\n- Counts existing owners in the request's city; if **\u2265 50** \u2192 **409** (`CityAtCapacityException`). (New owner not yet counted.)\n\n### 5. `EnsureDailyCreateLimit` \u2014 daily rate block\n- Determines the effective registration date (supplied, else today), rolled forward to a business day; if **\u2265 100** owners already carry that day \u2192 **429** (`DailyCreateLimitException`).\n\n### 6. `BuildOwner` \u2014 construct entity\n- Maps the validated DTO to an `Owner` and sets its `registrationDate` to the business-day-adjusted effective date.\n\n### 7. `AssignOwnerCustomerCode` \u2014 side-effect (in-memory mutation)\n- Assigns `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, where REGION is derived from the postcode and HASH8 is the first 8 upper-hex chars of SHA-256(canonical telephone + lastName). On collision with an existing code, appends `-<n>` (smallest n \u2265 2) for uniqueness.\n\n### 8. `AssignOwnerHousehold` \u2014 side-effect\n- Stamps the deterministic `householdId` (null when no postcode).\n\n### 9. `AssignOwnerNamesakeCount` \u2014 side-effect\n- Sets `namesakeCount` = number of existing owners (before this create) with the same firstName + lastName, case-insensitive.\n\n### 10. `SaveOwner` \u2014 persistence side-effect\n- Persists the owner (assigns its id).\n\n### 11. `RecordIdempotentCreate` \u2014 side-effect\n- If an `Idempotency-Key` was supplied, records `key \u2192 owner.id` so a later repeat returns this owner. No-op without a key.\n\n### 12. `AuditOwnerCreated` \u2014 side-effect\n- Emits an `AUDIT` log line with id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel, and derived membershipNumber.\n\n### 13. `AssignOwnerBulkSignupWarning` \u2014 side-effect (post-save, so counts itself)\n- Sets `bulkSignupWarning` = true when **> 80** owners share the registration day.\n\n### 14. `AssignOwnerHouseholdSize` \u2014 side-effect (post-save)\n- Sets transient `householdSize` = number of owners sharing the `householdId` (1 if no household); drives the GOLD tier (\u2265 3 members).\n\n### 15. `AssignOwnerPossibleDuplicate` \u2014 side-effect (post-save)\n- Sets transient `possibleDuplicate` / `possibleDuplicateOf`: true when another owner shares lastName (case-insensitive) + postcode but has a different canonical telephone, excluding same-household members; records the lowest-id match. False when no postcode or no match.\n\n### 16. `RespondWithOwnerCreated` \u2014 response\n- Maps to `OwnerDto` and responds **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n---\n\n**Notes:** Steps 3\u20135 are the ordered rejection gates (409/409/429) that run *after* body validation (400) but *before* the entity is built, so an invalid body always wins over a business-rule rejection. Steps 13\u201315 deliberately run after save so the newly created owner is counted, keeping the create response consistent with what a later `GET` recomputes. `householdSize`, `bulkSignupWarning`, `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf` are transient (recomputed, not persisted)."
  },
